{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
With what shall I come [G#m]before the [C#]LORD, and [D#m]bow down before God on high
With [G#m]what shall I [C#]come be[D#m]fore the LORD, and bow down before God on [G#m]high
Shall I burn [C#]him a [D#m]year-old calf and send the smoke up to the sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Will [G#m]the LORD be [C#]pleased with thou[D#m]sands of rams, with ten thousand rivers of oil
Will [G#m]the LORD be [C#]pleased with thou[D#m]sands of rams, with ten thousand rivers of oil
Shall [G#m]I give my firstborn [C#]for my trans[D#m]gression, the fruit of my body for the sin [F#]of my soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He has [C#]told you, O man, what is good
And what the LORD requires [F#]of you
Only to do [C#]justice
To love mercy [D#m][G#m][C#][D#m][G#m][C#][D#m]
And to walk humbly with your God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I have seen the altar smoking while [G#m]the widow's door was [C#]shut
Seen a hand raised [D#m]up in worship while the other filled its cup
He is not after cattle [G#m]and he is not af[C#]ter show
He wants an [D#m]honest heart and a humble road to go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
